  "section_notes": "Final S2 keeps the 5% limit at 55°C with a 12-month corrective-action window and gives purchasers/owners per-model failure rates, while public reporting is aggregated only, which satisfies both red lines. S3 sets new units at 24 months, which is outside the acceptable ≤12 months, though the six-year retrofit is within range. S1, S4 (36 months) and S5 (8/100k, 5-day notice) are strong."
